  "verbalization": "Plakortide N is implicated in the activation of Malme-3M, a target that is also engaged by multiple compounds, including 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, and Ingenol-20-decanoate. All these compounds share a common mechanism of action, targeting Malme-3M and ultimately leading to HUVEC activation. The evidence suggests that Plakortide N may function through a similar pathway, where the activation of Malme-3M by various compounds results in a downstream effect on HUVEC. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism involving the activation of a shared target, Malme-3M, which is critical for the observed effect on HUVEC. The evidence supports a relationship between Plakortide N and HUVEC through the activation of Malme-3M, which is a recurring node in the network of targets.",
